{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrzDWZ2kZUjBp7tj32yA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`get_metadata_for_wheel()` now only reads `METADATA` from a `.dist-info` directory at the root of the wheel. Nested ones, such as `pkg/_vendor/other-2.0.dist-info/`, are skipped. The fix is in `src/fromager/candidate.py`.\n\nI added `test_get_metadata_ignores_vendored_dist_info` to `tests/test_pep658_support.py`. It builds a wheel where the vendored `other` dist-info comes first in the archive, then checks that the root package's metadata is returned. With the fix, all 9 tests in that file pass. With the source change stashed, the new test fails and the other 8 pass.\n\nI took the first option from the issue (root-level only) rather than parsing the wheel filename to build `{dist_name}-{dist_version}.dist-info/METADATA`. A wheel with two dist-info directories at its root would still return the first one.\n\nI didn't run the formatter or linter: `ruff` isn't in `.venv`, so the new test lines may need `hatch run lint:fix`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3679,"cache_read_input_tokens":36993,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3679},"output_tokens":358,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd8c52d9-58ee-44ae-b557-a5450c6f2fbc","uuid":"69bfba82-7f9b-4bec-bb06-7816c3be0258","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:34:53.883Z","request_id":"req_011CfrzDWFgcuxwBSL8FcXyF"}
